'''Senate arcade building'''<ref name="Welcome AD">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> was an arcade located in the [[Imperial Plaza]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Ever" /> It was a predominantly [[Color|white]], sculptural structure defined by smooth curves and sharply cantilevered segments. Its design included an elevated promenade&mdash;a raised, linear walkway that follows the building's contours.<ref name="Welcome">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref> Additionally, the shaded gaps between the bases of its buttresses functioned as designated parking areas for [[senator]]ial [[limousine]]s.<ref name="Messenger">{{Andor|Messenger}}</ref>
{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:SenateArcadeIRL.jpg|thumb|left|200px|The real-life building used as the in-universe senate arcade building.]]
The senate arcade building first appeared in "[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]," the fourth episode of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''. The scenes involving the [[Imperial Plaza]] were shot in [[Wikipedia:Valencia|Valencia, Spain]] at the [[Wikipedia:City of Arts and Sciences|City of Arts and Sciences]] complex. Production designer [[Luke Hull]] felt that the architecture gave an "upper-Coruscant" look.<ref name="WorldofAndor">{{SWYouTube|sdMh_PoTpFo|Andor Season 2 &#124; The World of Andor &#124; Now Streaming on Disney+}}</ref> [[Industrial Light & Magic|ILM]] visual effects supervisor [[Mohen Leo]] overlaid the shooting location from Valencia into the layout of the [[Federal District|Senate District]] from the [[Prequel trilogy|prequels]] so that the senate arcade building and the wider Imperial Plaza would physically fit into what was previously established.<ref name="Week2Trivia">{{SW|url=news/andor-trivia-guide-week-2|text=Secrets from the Set of ''Andor'' Season 2: Week 2 Trivia}}</ref>

